  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plan and document:\r\rDesign and Access Statement\rHighway Safety Impact Form\rEnergy Statement\rLocation Plan\rExisting Block Plan\rProposed Block Plan\rExisting and Proposed Elevations and Sections\rExisting Plans\rProposed Plans\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes Order) 1 September 2020 (as Amended), the development shall only be used as a children's care home within Use Class C2 and for no other purpose whatsoever without express planning permission first being obtained from the Local Authority.\r\rReason: In the interests of residential amenity, car parking and highway safety.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be occupied by no more than 4 residents and 3 members of staff (excluding ad hoc visiting specialists/ therapists) at any one time.\r\rReason: To minimize the impact of the development on the occupiers of neighbouring properties and to ensure that car parking provision complies with the Council's adopted standards.",
    "Prior to occupation, unless otherwise agreed cycle parking should be provided in compliance with the following criteria:\r\rProvision of a minimum of TWO long stay cycle parking spaces in an accessible location: the access route to the store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free, close to the entrance and involve no more than 2 doors or gates (excluding the store door) which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m; secured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob; fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof. \r\rReason: The Council's Climate Action and Transport Policies seek to increase the use of active and sustainable transport modes. This means that access to bicycle parking should be easy and secure to remove potential barriers to cycling.",
    "Prior to first occupation, details of the design of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste shall be provided within the development in pursuance of the children's care home hereby approved, and in accordance with the London Borough of Enfield - Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). This shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority prior to occupation of the development. The facilities shall be provided in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In order to facilitate efficient, safe and clean removal of household refuse, the location and accessibility of refuse storage plus to maintain safety on the Highway.\r"
  ],
